## Divergence Time Estimation with SPNs ##
## constraining with secondary dates    ##
## obtained with Sanger sequencing      ##
##########################################

## Adapted from https://github.com/mmatschiner/tutorials/tree/master/divergence_time_estimation_with_snp_data
## .xml script will be generated using the ruby script 'snapp_prep.rb'
## SNPs dataset (in here we used low-coverage whole genome sequencing)
## based on dates estimated by Santos et al. 2022 (https://doi.org/10.1007/s11692-022-09583-z)

##########################
######    Step 1    ######
##########################

#create a constrain date and prior using nano (constrains.txt)

normal(0,11.2,3.4)    crown East_Xingu,Solimoes,Northern_AMZ,Upper_MAD,Middle_SEDI,Lower_TAP,Upper_TAP

#specify the prior distribution used, in our case 'normal' + offset = 0 + higher date + lower date
#named 'crown', since its divergence time estimated for all populations, followed by the name of all populations contained in the vcf

##########################
######    Step 2    ######
##########################

#create a tab delimited population file using nano, with the first column containing the populations and the second with the sample names

Cn  HT5206_Cn
Cn  MTR37449_Cn
Cn  MTR37484_Cn
Ex  BM133_Ex
Ex  BM316_Ex
Ex  MSH12664_Ex
Lm  H1106_Lm
Lm  H1480_Lm
Lm  MTR25696_Lm
Sol AOM182_Sol
Sol MTR35704_Sol
Sol MTR37100_Sol
Tap1    HT5219_Tap1
Tap1    HT9250_Tap1
Tap2    SJBH056_Tap2
Tap2    UFA090_Tap2
Tap2    LG1233_Tap2
Um  HERP5948_Um
Um  MTR13236_Um
Um  MTR19274_Um

##########################
######    Step 3    ######
##########################

#final command line
# -m = number of variant sites used from the .vcf dataset
# -l number of MCMC generations
# for more flags from the script use 'ruby snapp_prep.rb -h'

ruby snapp_prep.rb -v subset_snap_u_nomissing.vcf -t samples.txt -c constrainsts.txt -m 2000 -l 100000000 -x teste1_dating.xml

DONE!